From: nura-builds
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: commit planes after the modeset enables (bring-up)

On MDP5 v1.1 (MSM8226, Galaxy S III Neo) unblanking a DSI display crashed
in mdp5_crtc_atomic_flush() with an external abort on the LM registers:
the planes were committed (mixer setup, flush) before the modeset enables,
i.e. before the DSI bridge's pre_enable brought the DSI PLL, and with it
the pixel clock of the mixer/interface side, back. Use the order of
drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm(): disables, enables, planes (active
CRTCs only).
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_atomic.c
@@ -244,9 +244,15 @@
 	/*
 	 * Push atomic updates down to hardware:
 	 */
+	/*
+	 * Enables before planes (as drm_atomic_helper_commit_tail_rpm()): on MDP5 v1.1 (MSM8226) the
+	 * mixer and interface side needs the DSI PLL's pixel clock, which the DSI bridge only brings
+	 * back in its pre_enable; flushing planes into an enabling CRTC first aborts (external abort
+	 * on the LM registers after a blank/unblank)
+	 */
 	drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_disables(dev, state);
-	drm_atomic_helper_commit_planes(dev, state, 0);
 	drm_atomic_helper_commit_modeset_enables(dev, state);
+	drm_atomic_helper_commit_planes(dev, state, DRM_PLANE_COMMIT_ACTIVE_ONLY);
 
 	if (async) {
 		struct msm_pending_timer *timer =
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_crtc.c
@@ -565,6 +565,15 @@
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The irq masks from the new state: atomic_flush copies them too, but with the planes
+	 * committed after the modeset enables it runs after this, and the vblank irq would be
+	 * registered with an old (empty) mask: no vblank, page flips never complete
+	 */
+	mdp5_crtc->vblank.irqmask = mdp5_cstate->vblank_irqmask;
+	mdp5_crtc->err.irqmask = mdp5_cstate->err_irqmask;
+	mdp5_crtc->pp_done.irqmask = mdp5_cstate->pp_done_irqmask;
+
 	/* Restore vblank irq handling after power is enabled */
 	mdp5_crtc_vblank_on(crtc);
 
